Aim
To implement Prim’s algorithm to find a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) of a connected, weighted, undirected graph.
Theory
Prim’s algorithm starts from one vertex and repeatedly adds the minimum-weight edge that connects a vertex
already in the tree to a vertex outside it. It produces a minimum spanning tree for a connected, weighted, undirected
graph.
Algorithm
1. Read the number of vertices and the weighted adjacency matrix. Use 0 to represent no edge.
2. Mark vertex 0 as included in the MST.
3. Repeat until V − 1 edges have been selected: find the smallest edge from an included vertex to a non-included
vertex.
4. Add that edge to the MST, mark the new vertex as included, and add its weight to the total.
5. If no such edge exists before V − 1 edges are selected, the graph is disconnected.
Program (C)
#include <stdio.h>
#define MAX 100
#define INF 1000000000
int main(void) {
 int n, cost[MAX][MAX], selected[MAX] = {0};
 int edges = 0, total = 0;
 printf("Enter number of vertices: ");
 scanf("%d", &n);
 printf("Enter adjacency matrix (0 for no edge):\n");
 for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
 scanf("%d", &cost[i][j]);
 if (i != j && cost[i][j] == 0)
 cost[i][j] = INF;
 }
 }
 selected[0] = 1;
 printf("Edges in the Minimum Spanning Tree:\n");
 while (edges < n - 1) {
 int min = INF, u = -1, v = -1;
 for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 if (selected[i]) {
 for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
 if (!selected[j] && cost[i][j] < min) {
 min = cost[i][j];
 u = i;
 v = j;
 }
 }
 }
 }
 if (u == -1) {
 printf("Graph is disconnected; MST does not exist.\\n");
 return 0;
 }
 printf("%d - %d : %d\\n", u, v, min);
 total += min;
 selected[v] = 1;
 edges++; }
 printf("Total MST weight = %d\\n", total);
 return 0;
}
Sample Input
5
0 2 0 6 0
2 0 3 8 5
0 3 0 0 7
6 8 0 0 9
0 5 7 9 0
Sample Output
Edges in the Minimum Spanning Tree:
0 - 1 : 2
1 - 2 : 3
1 - 4 : 5
0 - 3 : 6
Total MST weight = 16
Time and Space Complexity
O(V²) using an adjacency matrix; auxiliary space O(V²) for the matrix and O(V) for the selected array.
Result
Prim’s algorithm was implemented and tested. It selected V − 1 minimum-weight edges and calculated the MST
cost.

